WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:24.000
Jonouchi vs Trap Deck

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:34.670
We will now pick who will duel in the second match.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.670
Start the Ultimate Bingo Machine!

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.550
The first duelist is #2!

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:56.960
Katsuya Jonouchi!

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.440
All right!

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.920
Who's my opponent?

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.540
His opponent is...

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.270
#7!

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.660
Marik Ishtar!

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.710
Marik?

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.140
Marik...  He's the duelist with the third God Card.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.530
He brainwashed Jonouchi and made us fight.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.590
Marik!  I'll defeat you with my own hands!

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.930
Begin the second match of the finals.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:44.480
Katsuya Jonouchi vs Marik Ishtar!

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.860
Listen, brainwash guy!

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.160
You humiliated us by breaking our bond of friendship!

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.160
I won't feel satisfied until I defeat you!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:04.520
I haven't seen him glare like that in a long time!

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.740
Yeah!  Jonouchi is fired up!

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.500
Yeah!  He's never lost when he's acting like this!

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.900
But I'm talking about fistfights.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:13.950
As expected.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.270
But Marik is also intimidating.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.780
He's clearly skilled.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.880
Don't let your guard down, Jonouchi.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.150
I'm getting nervous.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.550
Oh yeah.  Shizuka, you've never seen Jonouchi duel before.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:29.850
That's right.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.520
Cheer for him with all your might.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.530
Okay!

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.970
You've shuffled your deck enough.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.910
Take your positions.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.470
I will defeat that punk!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.740
I'm making a prediction!

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:53.680
Marik, you will lose on the 11th turn!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.460
11th turn?

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.560
Where did he get that number?

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.220
Wow, brother!

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.720
You've already calculated that?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.720
I think he just wanted to say those words.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.350
That's...

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.930
A Millennium Item!

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:18.600
Is Marik going to use it to brainwash Jonouchi again?

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.610
What's he up to?

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:32.400
He's going to duel fair and square for now.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.550
He is definitely Marik.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:44.600
The fake Millennium Rod is working well, Rishido.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.170
No one is doubting your identity.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:53.100
I failed to kill Yugi, but I have another big mystery to solve.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.080
You must pretend to be me until I find the answer.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.810
The big mystery is...

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:10.480
There's a priest facing the nameless Pharaoh on the tablet.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:15.280
He has Blue-Eyes and the Millennium Rod.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.960
Everything is similar.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.270
And he has Obelisk.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:28.910
Only those connected to the Millennium Items can use the God Cards.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.910
But that's not true for him.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.150
Rishido, distract him by pretending to be me.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:44.090
If you keep winning, there's a chance you'll cross paths with Kaiba.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.800
That's when I'll use the Millennium Rod to uncover his identity...

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:51.760
...for he holds the key to the outcome of the Millennium Battle.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:58.180
Big brother, does Marik really have the third God Card?

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:00.640
He does if he's the boss of the Ghouls.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:04.310
But I don't know for sure unless I see it with my own eyes.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:07.170
Jonouchi...

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:13.480
Be a good lab rat and make him play his God Card before you lose.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:18.930
Rishido, Jonouchi is a mediocre duelist.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:22.130
Against you, he's a little mouse.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:28.310
I know that I'm your decoy, Master Marik.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:33.820
I will bury whoever stands in your way.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.240
Here I go, Marik!

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.240
Duel!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.550
I go first!

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:50.690
I draw a card!

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:53.000
Go for it, Jonouchi!

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.140
I won't forgive you if you lose!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.470
By the way, did Jonouchi take back his Red-Eyes?

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:01.760
What?

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:05.200
He's playing without his trump card?

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:09.620
Jonouchi's deck doesn't have enough power.

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:15.510
He said that he'd take his card back when he became a true duelist.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:18.020
He thinks he's so cool!

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:23.220
I don't have Red-Eyes in my deck, but I'm still going to win!

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:27.280
I'll defeat Marik and take his God Card!

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:32.130
That means I'll be wielding a God Card!

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:42.920
That was close.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.140
I almost lost my valuable cards.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.660
Sheesh, brother!

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.220
Nice catch!

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:52.520
Sheesh.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.950
Even the wind is my enemy on the Battle Ship.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.390
Calm down, Jonouchi.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.620
Focus.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.680
It's my turn!

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.600
I'll play this!

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.720
Gearfried the Iron Knight in attack position!

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.500
That's a good card to start with!

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.580
Since I went first, I can't attack.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:17.570
I end my turn.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:18.940
My turn.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.640
I activate the Field Spell Temple of the Kings!

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.090
There's a temple on his field!

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:38.920
This field has become a sanctuary for the Pharaoh's treasures.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:44.030
All non-gravekeepers must now be humble.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.970
Humble?

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:51.690
Yes.  This card's effect limits the number of cards you can set per turn.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:52.770
What?

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:58.710
It stops you from removing the traps placed inside the temple.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.440
I end my turn.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:08.590
Jonouchi, are you brave enough to step into a sanctuary filled with traps?

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.080
Marik didn't summon a monster?

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.400
Then attack now!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.550
It won't work.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:14.570
Why not?

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:21.240
Marik didn't keep his traps a secret because he's confident that he'll catch Jonouchi.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.900
He can't attack carelessly.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:23.540
Damn!

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:27.810
I'm worried about that ark on the altar.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.810
What's inside?

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:36.530
Rishido, your traps are ready to make him suffer.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:38.960
This is scary...

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.050
Do your best, brother!

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.710
Don't be scared, Jonouchi!

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:43.880
Just kidding!

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:48.040
Those traps can't scare a man like me!

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:52.500
I have my special spell card, Giant Trunade.

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:58.110
If I play it, all spell and trap cards on the field return to our hands.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:03.550
He's planning to activate his trap when my monster attacks.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.380
So I won't attack.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:12.560
While he waits for me to attack, I'll summon as many monsters as possible.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:19.160
After he plays all the trap cards in his hand, I'll activate Giant Trunade.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:25.500
He'll have no cards on his field, and I'll attack with all my monsters.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.460
My strategy is perfect!

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:34.580
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:37.550
I summon Little-Winguard!

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.440
I end my turn.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.060
He's evaluating the situation.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:47.660
I'm getting very nervous.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.360
My turn.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.360
I set two more cards.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.300
I end my turn.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:57.860
He has four set cards.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:01.740
He's not summoning any monsters, focusing on a trap strategy.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:06.680
Just as I expected, Marik is only setting cards.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:07.840
My turn!

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.760
I summon another monster!

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:11.740
Come out!

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.890
Hayabusa Knight!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:21.190
My three monsters' combined attack points are over 4000.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:25.130
If I activate Giant Trunade this turn, I can defeat him instantly.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.570
Marik, you fell into my trap!

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:32.870
I activate the spell card Giant Trunade!

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:40.700
Nice!  He'll have no cards on his field!

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.280
Jonouchi wins!

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.220
What?

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:55.120
What happened?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:01.100
Jonouchi, you're the one who fell into a trap.

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:18.710
Giant Trunade's effect vanished.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:22.290
Why?

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:28.290
You thought my trap cards would activate if your monsters attacked.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:32.230
But I was waiting you to activate a spell card.

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:33.740
What?

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:40.280
I knew you had Giant Trunade because you didn't set any cards on your field.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:44.840
Giant Trunade would've returned them to your hand.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.550
He figured out my strategy.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:50.600
Humans are foolish.

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:57.390
They won't do extra work if they feel it's unnecessary, not realizing that will be their downfall.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:01.840
Jonouchi, your strategies aren't good enough to defeat me.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:06.970
This is the trap card I set for you!

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.760
Judgment of Anubis!

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:18.410
This trap card activates when you play a spell card.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:25.580
All monsters are destroyed, and you take damage equal to half their total attack points.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:26.820
What?

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:38.060
Your monsters' attack points equal 4200.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:42.430
So you lose 2100 life points.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.680
My monsters are all destroyed?

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:52.810
Jonouchi, you haven't faced my real trap yet.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.680
He summoned three monsters, but...

00:13:56.680 --> 00:14:00.980
Trap cards can turn the tables in an instant.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:06.290
And it deals emotional damage.

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:11.950
In the worst cases, you become so afraid of trap cards that you can't make a move.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:15.430
If this happens, you'll self-destruct.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:19.370
That's Marik's goal for his trap strategy.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:23.420
My brother is fine, right?

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.500
Y-Yeah.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.040
He's fine.  Right, Yugi?

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:31.360
Jonouchi won't run away from this.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:35.180
Traps won't break his fighting spirit.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.290
Brother, do you best!

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:39.150
Don't worry, Jonouchi!

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:43.500
Your turn isn't over yet.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:46.700
Listen, Marik.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:53.340
I deliberately fell for your traps this turn to see how skilled you are.

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:56.170
I underestimated you.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:15:01.820
You're the 21st duelist ever who's making me duel seriously.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.580
I'm now in serious mode!

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:07.620
I'm raising my duelist level to the max!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.240
Duelist level?  Max?

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:13.520
Great!  He wasn't dueling seriously yet!

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.460
He was at his limit...

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.750
Jonouchi...

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.460
He's something special.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.140
He's not discouraged.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:24.330
Because idiots don't feel pressure.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:28.200
Marik, it's your turn!  Bring it on!

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.320
My turn.  I draw.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.460
I set two more cards this turn.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.480
I end my turn.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:38.660
More set cards?

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.580
That's dirty!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.480
All you do is set traps!

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:45.700
You don't have the courage to fight fairly?

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:47.040
Coward!

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.060
Using traps is a fair strategy.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:52.480
You have no reason to call me a coward.

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:58.540
I'll show you why Duel Monsters is thrilling!

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:00.330
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:05.270
I summon Alligator's Sword in attack position!

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:11.920
His five set cards are definitely traps.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:15.320
If I attack carelessly, his traps will get me.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:16.920
What's wrong?

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:20.890
I thought you were going to show me why duels are thrilling.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.820
Damn!  I can't afford to attack.

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:26.370
I also set one card.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:27.540
I end my turn.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.450
That's the right decision.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:35.200
If you act, you'll get caught in Marik's trap.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.740
You have to wait for your chance.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:39.840
It's your turn.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:43.680
I end my turn without doing anything.

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:47.660
Damn!  He's waiting for me to attack.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.350
But I won't fall for it!

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.900
I also end my turn!

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:55.020
It's my turn.  I draw.

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.960
I end my turn.

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:02.140
Big brother, his strategy is obvious.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:06.910
If neither attacks, this match will never end.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:08.620
That's not true.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:13.170
The pressure will act as a stimulant for that idiot's brain.

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.940
Marik!

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:18.060
Oh no!

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:20.400
Jonouchi, don't lose your cool!

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:21.820
That's what Marik wants!

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:22.840
Be quiet!

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:24.220
My turn!

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.060
I summon Rocket Warrior!

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.180
I've had it!

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:35.620
My pride as a duelist won't allow you to avoid confrontation!

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:39.840
As promised, I'll show you why duels are thrilling!

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.640
Rocket Warrior transforms into Invincible Mode!

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:46.350
Attack him directly!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.540
No, Jonouchi!

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:52.910
I activate my trap card!

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:56.450
Eye of Ujat!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:07.390
I gain control of the monster marked with the Eye of Ujat for one turn.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.330
What?

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:12.280
Rocket Warrior, attack Alligator's Sword!

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:16.600
I knew you'd do that!

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:18.340
I activate my spell card!

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:20.860
Fairy Box!

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.510
That weird box hid his monster.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:32.450
Rocket Warrior lost track of its target.

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:37.050
There!  Rocket Warrior!

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:39.930
Did I destroy it?

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:45.820
What?

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:50.400
Too bad!  My monster is fine!

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:55.400
And I learned your trap strategy's weakness!

00:18:57.930 --> 00:19:03.750
Your deck only has spell and trap cards.

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:07.350
You don't have a single monster card.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:12.480
No matter what traps you set, if I destroy them...

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:18.530
...I can easily erase your life points because you have no monsters to defend with.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:21.970
You're struggling because you're failing to do that!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:24.970
Jonouchi, are you sure about that?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:28.450
You're already caught in my swarm of traps.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:29.410
What?

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:32.340
Rishido, end this soon.

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:35.280
Stop playing around with him.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:41.640
As you've pointed out, my deck mostly contains trap and spell cards.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:47.420
But what if there's a trap card that acts as a monster card?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.680
A trap card that acts as a monster card?

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:56.370
If such a card exists, the powerful deck will overcome its weaknesses.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:57.640
Such a card...

00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:59.070
...actually exists?

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:04.400
I'll show you the card that punishes those who tarnish God's sanctuary!

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:08.510
This trap card has already activated this turn.

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.370
What?

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:15.730
The trap monster card Embodiment of Apophis!

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:20.890
This trap activates when you attack.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:26.770
Its effect summons Apophis, a monster that protects God.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:33.060
No way!  When that trap activates, it summons a monster?

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:36.920
Jonouchi attacked with Rocket Warrior this turn.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:41.150
Since he did, the trap will activate and summon a monster.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:46.320
I set three copies of that trap card.  So...

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:52.400
Three monsters will be summoned this turn!

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.940
Come out, Apophis!

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:07.570
Three monsters at once?

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.220
Wow...

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.220
He's done for.

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:13.450
So this is Marik's trap strategy.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:16.110
This is what he was aiming for!

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:25.370
Jonouchi, you're a poor mouse that walked into my swarm of traps.

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:28.330
Prepare to fall into the abyss.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:47.730
The trap monsters' attacks have put Jonouchi in a huge pinch!

00:21:47.730 --> 00:21:49.800
Is there nothing you can do?

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:53.170
Jonouchi, it's not like you to surrender!

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:57.400
The winning duelists carry on the dreams of those who lost.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:22:00.640
Mai's words inspire Jonouchi to stand again.

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:05.550
That's right!  You have to fight for those you defeated, like Roba and Kajiki!

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.370
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Inherited Card
Jinzo's Counterattack!

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:10.880
Duel, standby!

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:21.930
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:30.870
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:35.840
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:39.810
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:47.790
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:51.360
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:56.130
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:56.130 --> 00:23:06.240
And walk it without stopping

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:13.850
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:22.820
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:30.800
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:40.640
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
